<title>ITALY: Prodi, other leaders meet on employment.</title>
<headline>Prodi, other leaders meet on employment.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Political parties supporting Prime Minister Romano Prodi's coalition began a meeting on Thursday to discuss government plans to boost employment.</p>
<p>The meeting included ministers in Prodi's cabinet as well as Fausto Bertinotti, leader of the hard-left Communist Refoundation, which supports the government in parliament.</p>
<p>Prodi's office also announced that the cabinet will meet at 0830 GMT on Friday to discuss employment and other items.</p>
<p>Rome newsroom +396-6782501</p>
